### Assignment 9 test requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension, or Postman)

### All books with stock
GET http://localhost:3000/books

### One book
GET http://localhost:3000/books/3

### Customer 2's orders
GET http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders

### Q2 - place an order (customer 2 buys 2 copies of book 3)
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 3, "quantity": 2 }

### Q3 - not enough stock (book 5 has only 4 copies) -> expect 409
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 5, "quantity": 5 }

### Q4 - customer 999 does not exist -> INSERT fails -> stock must be unchanged
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/999/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 1, "quantity": 1 }

### Q5 - cancel an order (replace 8 with the id that Q2 returned)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders/7

### Q5 - cancel an order that doesn't exist -> expect 404
DELETE http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders/9999
